  "description": "Na₃SbO₃ crystallizes in the cubic I̅43m space group. Na¹⁺ is bonded to five equivalent O²⁻ atoms to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing NaO₅ square pyramids. There are a spread of Na-O bond distances ranging from 2.36-2.42 Å. Sb³⁺ is bonded in a distorted trigonal non-coplanar geometry to three equivalent O²⁻ atoms. All Sb-O bond lengths are 1.96 Å. O²⁻ is bonded to five equivalent Na¹⁺ and one Sb³⁺ atom to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing ONa₅Sb octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles are 19°.",
